# App Idea: "Mood Palette" – A Color-Based Mood Tracker

**Concept:**  
"Mood Palette" is a unique, visually engaging desktop app that lets users log and visualize their daily moods using colors. Instead of traditional text-based mood tracking, users select a color from a professional palette that best represents their current mood. Over time, the app builds a beautiful calendar grid of colored squares—one for each day—allowing users to see patterns in their emotional well-being at a glance.

---

## Features

- Modern, minimalist interface with professional color schemes.
- Customizable color palette representing different moods.
- Calendar view showing each day's selected mood as a colored square.
- Hover/click on any day to see details or edit the entry.
- Uses clean fonts and subtle frames for an elegant look.

---

## Code

```python
import tkinter as tk
from tkinter import ttk
from datetime import date, timedelta

# Professional color palette (mood colors)
MOOD_COLORS = [
    ("Joyful", "#FFD700"),   # Gold
    ("Calm", "#87CEEB"),     # Sky Blue
    ("Energetic", "#FF6347"),# Tomato Red
    ("Relaxed", "#98FB98"),  # Pale Green
    ("Sad", "#778899"),      # Slate Gray
    ("Anxious", "#FFB6C1")   # Light Pink
]

FONT_TITLE = ('Segoe UI', 18, 'bold')
FONT_DAY = ('Segoe UI', 10)
FRAME_BG = '#F5F6FA'
CAL_BG = '#FFFFFF'
SELECTED_BORDER = '#2D9CDB'

class MoodPaletteApp(tk.Tk):
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__()
        self.title("Mood Palette")
        self.configure(bg=FRAME_BG)
        self.resizable(False, False)

        self.moods_by_day = {}  # {date: (color_name,color_hex)}

        title_label = tk.Label(self,
                               text="Mood Palette",
                               font=FONT_TITLE,
                               bg=FRAME_BG,
                               fg="#222831")
        title_label.pack(pady=(20,10))

        desc_label = tk.Label(self,
                              text="Select your daily mood by choosing a color.\nSee your month at-a-glance.",
                              font=('Segoe UI', 11),
                              bg=FRAME_BG,
                              fg="#393E46")
        desc_label.pack()

        cal_frame = tk.Frame(self,bg=CAL_BG,borderwidth=2,relief='groove')
        cal_frame.pack(padx=30,pady=(15,10))

        self.cal_frame = cal_frame
        
        controls_frame=tk.Frame(self,bg=FRAME_BG)
        
        controls_frame.pack()
        
        today_btn=tk.Button(controls_frame,text="Today ▶",
                            command=self.set_today_mood,font=('Segoe UI',9,'bold'),
                            bg='#2D9CDB',fg='white',
                            relief='flat')
        
        today_btn.grid(row=0,column=len(MOOD_COLORS)+1,padx=(8),pady=(8))
```

